  'twitchGuide.title': 'How to Watch Multiple Twitch Streams at Once',
  'twitchGuide.excerpt': 'Put several Twitch streams side by side for free — no account, no extension. Add channels by name, let the grid arrange them, keep chat on screen and share the whole line-up as one link.',
  'twitchGuide.why': 'Why watch several Twitch streams together',
  'twitchGuide.why.desc': 'Esports matches with player POVs, a collab where every streamer has their own camera, or simply following a few favourite channels while they are all live — sometimes one stream is not enough. Instead of juggling browser tabs, MultiStream Hub puts every Twitch player on one canvas, each with its own volume, with chat right next to them.',
  'twitchGuide.steps': 'Watch multiple Twitch streams in three steps',
  'twitchGuide.steps.1': 'Open the canvas and paste a Twitch link (twitch.tv/channel) or simply type the channel name into the search box. Live status shows up as you type, so you can see who is on air before adding them.',
  'twitchGuide.steps.2': 'Keep adding channels — up to 16 at once. The grid rearranges itself automatically; drag, resize or enlarge any window, and give each stream its own volume so you only hear the one you are focused on.',
  'twitchGuide.steps.3': 'Add chat windows if you want them (the “Chat Included” layouts place them in one click), then press the share button to copy the whole line-up as a single link.',
  'twitchGuide.example': 'Try it: open three Twitch channels from one link',
  'twitchGuide.example.desc': 'This link opens three Twitch channels side by side. Swap in the channel names you want — tw: stands for Twitch, and channels are separated by commas.',
  'twitchGuide.example.share': 'The share guide explains the full link format, including YouTube streams and the 16-stream limit.',
  'twitchGuide.example.shareLink': 'Read the share guide',
  'twitchGuide.multitwitch': 'How it compares with MultiTwitch',
  'twitchGuide.multitwitch.desc': 'MultiTwitch made the idea popular: add channel names to the URL and watch them in an equal split. MultiStream Hub covers the same ground without an account, and adds YouTube streams next to Twitch, a free-drag canvas, per-stream and master volume, favourites that import your Twitch follows and detect when channels go live, five interface languages and mobile support.',
  'twitchGuide.multitwitch.more': 'Want the full picture, including TwitchTheater and Multistre.am?',
  'twitchGuide.multitwitch.moreLink': 'See the comparison',
  'twitchGuide.faq': 'Common questions',
  'twitchGuide.faq.q1': 'Is it free?',
  'twitchGuide.faq.a1': 'Yes. Watching multiple Twitch streams is completely free, with no sign-up and nothing to install.',
  'twitchGuide.faq.q2': 'How many Twitch streams can I watch at once?',
  'twitchGuide.faq.a2': 'Up to 16. How smooth it feels depends on your computer and connection — mute or lower the quality of the streams you are not watching closely.',
  'twitchGuide.faq.q3': 'Can I follow chat too?',
  'twitchGuide.faq.a3': 'Yes. Add chat windows next to the players — the “Chat Included” layouts arrange them for you — and keep up with the conversation while you watch.',
  'twitchGuide.faq.q4': 'Does it work on a phone?',
  'twitchGuide.faq.a4': 'Yes, it runs in mobile browsers too, though a computer or tablet gives you more room for several streams at once.',
